MiBench is a benchmark suite for embedded devices. bin folder has the ARM binaries.
input_data has the inputs and input_generation generates inputs for all bmrks.

Explaination to run benchmarks:

Automotive/industrial:
1. basicmath: simple math calculations. ./basicmath_ARM 1
2. bitcount: # bits in array of integers. ./bitcount_ARM 2
3. qsort: quicksort. ./qsort_small_ARM 3 ../input_data/qsort_small_input.txt
4. Susan: Image recognition. Vision based quality assurance. ./susan_ARM ../input_data/susan_input.pgm out.pmg
Network:
5. dijstra: Graph. ./dijkstra_ARM 3 ../input_data/dijkstra_input.dat  (SEGFAULTS)
6. particia:  Patricia tries are used to represent routing tables in network applications. ./patricia_ARM ../input_data/patricia_input.udp 
Security:
8. sha: Secure hash algorithm. DOES NOT RUN
9. rijndael encrypt/decrypt: does not build
10. pgp: Dos not build
Consumer Devices:
11. jpeg encode/decode: ./cjpeg_ARM ../input_data/jpeg_input.ppm 
12. tiff: None build. Will spend time later.
13. lame: MP3 decoder. Buffer overflow on normal CPU
14. mad: Mad is a high-quality MPEG audio decoder.Does not build
15. typeset: Typeset is a general typesetting tool, that has a front-end processor for HTML. Check run_typeset.sh. All libs are the in the typeset folder (bin/typeset)
Office:
16. ghostscript: Does not build
17. stringsearch: This benchmark searches for given words in phrases using a case insensitive comparison algorithm. ./stringsearch_ARM 1
18. ispell: Does not build
19. rsynth: Does not run?
20. sphinx: Sphinx is a speech decoder that operates on finite-length segments of speech or utterances, one utterance at a time. Segfault
21. FFT: ./fft_ARM 10 2
22. GSM: Video encoding/decoding. run_gsm.sh
23. ADPCM: Adaptive Differential Pulse Code Modulation. run_adpcm.sh.

